Package: codetopo
Title: Code Topology Analysis from R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Nrupal", "Akolkar",
    email = "51525601+nrupala@users.noreply.github.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R surface over the codetopo Rust core, built with extendr.
  Index a repository into a queryable code graph, then search, trace,
  rank, and render it — deterministically and read-only. All answers are
  CODE_SCHEMA (v1.2) JSON produced by the same Rust library the CLI, HTTP,
  and MCP surfaces serve, so the R face agrees with them by construction.
  This package lives in the codetopo repository only; it is not published
  to CRAN.
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports: jsonlite
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager) and Rust; the crate
  'libR-sys' must compile without error
Config/rextendr/version: 0.5.0
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
